    "id": "rate_half_ca_hankel_a1_core_one_exceptional_only_distance_three_generic_schur_defect_trigonal_fiber_classification",
    "title": "Rate-half distance-three generic Schur-defect trigonal-fiber classification",
    "status": "PROVED",
    "closure": "proof",
    "statement": "On the rank-three pair-locator branch, let V=span{A,B A/D_i}. The exact defect (3e+1)-dim(VV) equals the dimension of the linear solution space of D_i | R-y_iB with deg R<=2, and that solution space has dimension at most one. Thus the generic quadratic rank is exactly 3e+1 or 3e; in the latter case all but at most one pair lie in distinct fibers of one projectively unique recovered degree-three rational map B/R. On official active rows, dim(VV) is exactly the quadratic locator-matrix rank.",
